subject Fix parenthesis in generator proof

The definition of S_Y has an unmatched closing parenthesis after phi. The predicate is simply that phi factors through Y; this also agrees with the corresponding argument in Tohoku section 1.9, printed page 134.

diff --git a/injectives.tex b/injectives.tex
index 1b24742..a9e1347 100644
--- a/injectives.tex
+++ b/injectives.tex
@@ -1368,7 +1368,7 @@ Part (2) follows from the definition of cofinality and (1).
 \medskip\noindent
 Proof of (3). For any subobject $Y \subset X$
 define $S_Y \in \mathcal{P}(\Mor(U, X))$ (power set) as
-$S_Y = \{\phi \in \Mor(U,X) : \phi)\text{ factors through }Y\}$.
+$S_Y = \{\phi \in \Mor(U,X) : \phi\text{ factors through }Y\}$.
 Then $Y = Y'$ if and only if $S_Y = S_{Y'}$. Hence the cardinality
 of the set of subobjects is at most the cardinality of this power set.
 \end{proof}
